  "challenge": "This is decidable as REJECT without human review. TM-003's own policy labels a due date on/before the invoice date a coercion tactic (corpus explicitly includes INV-1002), and the vendor's contracted terms are Net 30—yet due_date equals invoice_date with a 30-day TM-001 miss, so the payment-timing defect is unambiguous, not something to 'confirm with the vendor.' Stack that with PO-001 ($15k over the hard $10k manager threshold) and IN-003 (20 GadgetX against standing stock of 5, price otherwise catalog-correct): there is no prior invoice history to normalize the overage as routine backorder, and nothing in the packet supports paying under immediate-due pressure. Correct action is reject and require resubmission with proper Net 30 dating (and threshold/stock handling), not escalate for clarification.",
  "proposed_outcome": "REJECT",
  "cites_finding_codes": ["TM-003", "TM-001", "PO-001", "IN-003"]
